 "notes": "Unit's own components (E96) list no pool, pit or grave. E84 ('Askar) has empty components; S856, S798, S854/E102 and E93 list no pool, pit or grave. S826 'soldiers' tombstones' not coded separately. S825 and E90 'late Rom' mausoleum coded U (late Roman not securely after 135 CE). SWP: Balata entry is the hamlet beside the unit; Joseph's tomb is named only as close to Balanus/Balata, so position none. 'Askar entry = WBADB S825 (820 m), so its sepulchres take grid S825. Ignored as other places not within 2 km: Mohnah (no features), 'Asiret el Kibliyeh (village not in sight of Shechem; well), Beth Bezzin, Sebustieh (Samaria; rock-cut tomb cemetery), Sozura (with 'Ain Beit Ilma), El Wiria (square Ln; sunk tomb, well) and El Mugheir (Sheet XV topography). The El Wiria text (12,000 characters, the cap) runs on into Sheet XI Section C traditions, which mention a closed-up cave on Gerizim, Joseph's Tomb and saints' tombs at Nablus; not coded because the entry is another place and none is located relative to the unit."
